{
	title: 'Supervised server mode',
	spec: 'Hal supports hostMode auto (default peer promotion) or server in config.ason. In server mode ordinary terminals and print clients never acquire the host lock, even after loss or restart; they wait and reconnect. Invalid hostMode values refuse local client startup rather than silently permitting promotion. hal serve explicitly starts the foreground headless host without a terminal, using the existing exclusive lock, web service, recovery, plugins and version reporting. A competing host causes a clear startup failure. SIGHUP does not stop the headless host; SIGTERM/SIGINT stop it without recording user pauses; SIGUSR1 and /restart preserve intentional restart exit 100. Supervision, not custom daemonization, manages lifetime. Tests cover a real headless host, hangup survival, single ownership and client reconnection without promotion. Session-state documentation distinguishes server mode from automatic peer mode.',
